@startuml seller-onboarding
!include ../_theme.puml
title Seller onboarding

' Derived from: wovely AuthController#registerUser, config/DataSeeder; frontend register.component.ts,
' seller-inventory.component.ts, settings.component.ts; products services/ListingService, AdminProductController
|Seller|
start
:Open "Join" and choose\n"Shop and sell my work";
|SPA|
:POST /api/auth/signup\nroles ["seller"];
|Core service|
if (Valid, unique, roles only "user" / "seller"?) then (no)
  :400 with the reason;
  stop
else (yes)
  :Account gets ROLE_SELLER;
endif
|Seller|
:Log in;
:Add workshop city, photo and story in Settings;
:Add a product with stock and delivery details;
|Products service|
:Save as PENDING and register stock with inventory;
note right
  Self-service seller accounts are safe because
  nothing reaches buyers before a moderator
  approves the listing.
end note
|Admin|
repeat
  :Review the listing;
  if (Decision?) then (approve)
    |Products service|
    :APPROVED: listing joins the catalog;
    |Seller|
    :Receive orders;
    stop
  elseif (reject) then
    |Products service|
    :REJECTED (final; edits return 409);
    |Seller|
    stop
  else (request changes)
    |Products service|
    :NEEDS_CHANGES;
    |Seller|
    :Edit the listing ("Changes requested" badge);
    |Products service|
    :Back to PENDING (PRODUCT_RESUBMITTED);
  endif
  |Admin|
repeat while (Back in the queue)
@enduml
